          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em locally presentable category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            which contains a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+objects"} small objects
            such that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            is a nice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over objects in this set.
          %p
            This says equivalently that a locally presentable category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+localization"} reflective localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \hookrightarrow PSh(S)
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(S)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+colimit+completion"} free colimit completion
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            and the localization imposes
            = succeed "," do
              %em relations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            by
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generators+and+relations"} generators and relations
            = succeed "." do
              %em (locally) presentable category
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories+-+introduction"} locally presentable categories - introduction
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are many equivalent characterizations of
            = succeed "." do
              %em locally presentable categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EquivalentCharacterizations"} below
          #PresentableCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (locally presentable category)
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is called
              %strong locally presentable
              if
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  it is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible category
              %li
                %p
                  it has all small
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %p This means
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  is a
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  has all small
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
              %li
                %p
                  there exists a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi S
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi Obj
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \hookrightarrow Obj(\mathcal{C})
                  of
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact
                  objects that generates
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  under
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                  for some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi λ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              If follows that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              in a locally presentable category is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
          %p
          #Terminology.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The
              %em locally
              in
              %em locally presentable category
              refers to the fact that it is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              of (in) the category that are presentable, not the category as such (which is itself an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              of
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+presentable+objects"} finitely presentable objects
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Since a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+object"} small object
              is one which is
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "-compact" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "-compact" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda \gt \kappa
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              such that every object of the colimit-generating set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is
              = succeed "-compact." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p This provides a “stratification” of the class of locally presentable categories, as follows.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (locally
                = succeed "-presentable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              %strong
                locally
                = succeed "-presentable" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              is a locally presentable category, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresentableCategory"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              may be taken to consist of
              = succeed "-compact" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              Thus, a locally presentable category is one which is locally
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %em some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              (hence also for every
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda\gt\kappa
              = succeed "-compact" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              = succeed "-compact" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              (though there is no uniform upper bound on the required size of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi λ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+generator"} strong generator
              consisting of small objects.
          #LocallyFinitelyPresentable.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A locally
              = succeed "-presentable" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℵ
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\aleph}_0
              = succeed "." do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+category"} locally finitely presentable category
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#EquivalentCharacterizations Equivalent characterizations
          %p There are various equivalent characterizations of locally presentable categories.
          %h4#as_limitpreserving_functor_categories As limit-preserving functor categories
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (as limit sketches)
            %p
              Locally presentable categories are precisely the categories of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sketch"} models of limit-sketches
          %p
            This is
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AdámekRosický94"} Adámek &amp; Rosický (1994), corollary 1.52
          %p Restricted to locally finitely presentable categories this becomes:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Locally finitely presentable categories, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFinitelyPresentable"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limit"} finite limit
              preserving functors
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to Set
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            For the more detailed statement see below at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "#GabrielUlmerDuality"} Gabriel-Ulmer duality
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Locally finitely presentable categories are equivalently
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
              of finitary
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+algebraic+theories"} essentially algebraic theories
          %h4#AsLocalizationsOfPresheafCategories As localizations of presheaf categories
          #AsLocalizationOfPresheafCategories.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (as accessible reflective subcategories of presheaves)
            %p
              Locally presentable categories are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessibly embedded
              full
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategories"} reflective subcategories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi C
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi i
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi L
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (L \dashv i)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    C
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{i}{\hookrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{L}{\leftarrow}}
                    {\;\;\bot\;\;}
                    PSh(K)
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+of+presheaves"} categories of presheaves
              on some small category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
          %p
            This appears as
            %a{:href => "#AdámekRosický94"} Adámek &amp; Rosický (1994), prop 1.46
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#GabrielUlmer"} Gabriel &amp; Ulmer (1971), Satz 8.5(c) and Bemerkung 8.6(c)
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              Here
              %em accessibly embedded
              means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \hookrightarrow Psh(K)
              is an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is closed in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(K)
              under
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
              for some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
          %p
            See also at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes+are+equivalently+the+left+exact+reflective+subcategories+of+presheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes are equivalently the left exact reflective subcategories of presheaf toposes
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              Locally presentable categories are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+category"} complete
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              A reflective subcategory of a complete category is complete, since
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functors
              reflect limits, and the above proposition shows that any locally presentable category is a reflective subcategory of a presheaf category, which is complete.
          %h3#GabrielUlmerDuality Finite presentability and Gabriel–Ulmer duality
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Lex
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lex
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+categories"} small categories
              with
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+limits"} finite limits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              between them, and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
              between those.
            %p
              Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi LFP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} LFP
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
              of locally finitely presentable categories, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFinitelyPresentable"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              functors which preserve
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
          .num_prop
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel-Ulmer+duality"}> Gabriel-Ulmer duality
                )
            %p
              There is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+2-categories"} equivalence of 2-categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Lex
                      %mi op
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %mi LFP
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Lex^{op} \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} LFP
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi Lex
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C \mapsto Lex(C,Set)
            %p
              which sends a finitely complete category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              to the category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/models"} models
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functors"} left exact functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h3#wellpoweredness_and_wellcopoweredness Well-poweredness and well-copoweredness
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"} locally presentable category
                is well-powered, since it is a full reflective subcategory of a presheaf topos, so its subobject lattices are subsets of those of the latter.
            %li
              %p
                Every locally presentable category is also well-
                %em> copowered
                \. This is shown in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#AdámekRosický94"} Adámek &amp; Rosický (1994), Prop. 1.57 &amp; Thm. 2.49
          %h3#tensor_product Tensor product
          %p
            The category of locally presentable categories is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
            structure, defined by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi D
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Cts
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \otimes D := Cts(C^op, D)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cts
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cts
            denotes the 2-category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+categories"} complete categories
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functors"} continuous functors
            (
            %a{:href => "#Bird82"}> Bird 1982
            ): see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pr%28infinity%2C1%29Cat"} Pr(infinity,1)Cat
            for more details.
          %h2#examples_and_applications Examples and applications
          %h3#locally_finitely_presentable_categories Locally finitely presentable categories
          %p
            We list examples of locally finitely presentable categories, def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LocallyFinitelyPresentable"}
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
              is locally finitely presentable.
            %p
              For notice that every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimit"} directed colimit
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              of all its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            %p
              Moreover, a set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in Set
              is a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
              precisely if it has cardinality
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &lt;
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |S| \lt \kappa
              = succeed "-compact." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/aleph"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℵ
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0
            %p
              Hence a a set of generators that exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              as a locally finitely complete category is given by the set containing one finite set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              More generally, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^C
              is locally finitely presentable.
            %p
              This follows with
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel-Ulmer+duality"} Gabriel-Ulmer duality
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lex+completion"} finite limit completion
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Lex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lex(C)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^C
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
              to the category of finitely continuous functors
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Lex
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lex(C) \to Set
          .num_example
            %h6#example_3 Example
            %p
              More generally still, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is locally finitely presentable and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^C
              is locally finitely presentable.
            %p
              To see this, embed
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} finitely-accessible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^B
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functor"} 2-functoriality
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^C
              we get
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^C
              as a finitely-accessible reflective subcategory of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mo ×
                          %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{B \times C}
          .num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+Lawvere+theory"} algebras of
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is finitely presented if and only if the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Alg_T(A, -)
              preserves
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+an+algebraic+theory"} algebra
              can be expressed as a filtered colimit of finitely presented algebras.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The category of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coalgebras"} coalgebras
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is locally finitely presentable; similarly the category of commutative coalgebras over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is locally finitely presentable.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
              which is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+lattice"} algebraic
              (each element is a directed
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
              of finite elements).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counter-examples"}> counter-examples
                )
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  The category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinSet"} FinSet
                  of
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
                  sets is
                  %em not
                  locally finitely presentable, as it does not have all countable colimits.
              %li
                %p
                  The category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Field"} Field
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
                  and field
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                  is
                  %em not
                  locally presentable, as it does not have all binary coproducts (for instance, there are none between fields of differing characteristics).
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TopologicalSpaces"} TopologicalSpaces
                  is not locally finitely presentable.
              %li
                %p
                  The
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
                  of a locally presentable category (in particular, a locally finitely presentable category) is
                  %em never
                  locally presentable, unless it is a poset. This is
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a{:href => "#GabrielUlmer"} Gabriel-Ulmer, Satz 7.13
            %p
          %h3#locally_presentable_categories Locally presentable categories
          .num_example
            %h6#example_5 Example
            %p
              A
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
          %p
          #GrothAbCatsAreLocPresntbl.num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+abelian+category"} Grothendieck abelian category
              is locally presentable &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#Beke00"}> Beke (200), Prop. 3.10
              , cf.
              = succeed "&rbrack;." do
                %a{:href => "#Krause15"} Krause (2015), Cor. 5.2
            %p
              This implies in particular (by
              %a{:href => "Grothendieck+category#ChainComplexesInGrothAbCat"} this example
              at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+abelian+category"} Grothendieck abelian category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to any
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topos"} Grothendieck topos
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
                  of
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi R
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
                  is locally presentable
              %li
                %p
                  the category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+chain+complexes"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Ch
                            %mo •
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi R
                          %mi Mod
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ch_\bullet(R Mod)
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
                  is locally presentable.
            %p
          .num_example
            %h6#example_6 Example
            %p
              The following three examples, being
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+categories"} presheaf categories
              %em a fortiori
              locally presentable. They are important for the general study of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              %li
                %p
                  the category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dSet"} dSet
                  of
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+sets"} dendroidal sets
              %li
                %p
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Funct
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi C
                        %mo ,
                        %mi sSet
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Funct(C,sSet)
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaves"} simplicial presheaves
                %p
                  (see Prop.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PresheavesWithValuesInLocPresAreLocPres"}
                  below).
          %p More generally,
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              is locally presentable.
          %p
            This appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Borceux"}> Borceux, prop. 3.4.16, page 220
            ). It follows directly with prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AsLocalizationOfPresheafCategories"}
            and using that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            is an accessibly embedded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtopos"} subtopos
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
            (see at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+toposes+are+equivalently+the+left+exact+reflective+subcategories+of+presheaf+toposes"} sheaf toposes are equivalently the left exact reflective subcategories of presheaf toposes
          %p The main ingredient of a direct proof is:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_5 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              strictly larger than the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mor
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mor(C)
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(C)
              is computed objectwise.
          %p
            This implies that all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf+topos"} sheaf topos
            are
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+objects"} compact objects
          #AlgebrasOverAnAccessibleMonad.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+monad"} accessible monad
              (a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
              whose underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              is an
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^T
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+a+monad"} algebras over the monad
              is locally presentable. In particular, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is locally presentable and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i: B \to A
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is locally presentable if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is accessible.
          %p
            This appears in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AdámekRosický94"} Adámek &amp; Rosický (1994), 2.78
          .query
            %p This is actually somewhat subtle and gets into some transfinite combinatorics, from what I can gather.
          %p
          #PresheavesWithValuesInLocPresAreLocPres.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p Given
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                  a locally presentable category
            %p
              then also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{A})
              is locally presentable.
          This is
          %a{:href => "#AdámekRosický94"} Adámek &amp; Rosický (1994), Cor. 1.54
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/functor+category#LocalPresentability"} Functor category – Local presentability
            for more.
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              of a locally presentable category is again locally presentable.
            %p
          This appears for instance as
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "#CentazzoRosickyVitale"} Centazzo-Rosický-Vitale, remark 3
          %p
          #LocallyPresentableGrothendieckConstruction.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (locally presentable Grothendieck constructions)
              %br/
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudofunctor"} pseudofunctor
              with values in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CatAdj"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cat
                        %mi Adj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{Adj}
              as
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi C
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi Base
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                            %mi Cat
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒳
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi C
                              %mi 𝒳
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mo
                                  %mrow
                                    %msup
                                      %mi f
                                      %mo *
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↑
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi f
                                      %mo !
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝒴
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↦
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi C
                              %mi 𝒴
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\mathllap{
                    \\mathbf{C} \,\colon\,
                    \\;
                    }
                    Base &amp;\longrightarrow&amp; Cat
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{X} &amp;\mapsto&amp; \mathbf{C}_{\mathcal{X}}
                    \\\
                    \\Big\downarrow\mathrlap{{}^{f}}
                    \&amp;&amp;
                    \\mathllap{^{f^\ast}}\Big\uparrow
                    \\Big\downarrow\mathrlap{{}^{f_!}}
                    \\\
                    \\mathcal{Y} &amp;\mapsto&amp; \mathbf{C}_{\mathcal{Y}}
                    }
            %p
              such that for some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} regular cardinal
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Base
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Base
                  is locally
                  = succeed "-presentable," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %li
                %p
                  each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi C
                          %mi 𝒳
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}_{\mathcal{X}}
                  is locally presentable,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{C}_{(-)}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+colimit"} preserves
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                    \-filtered
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limits"} 2-limits
            %p
              then also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+construction"} Grothendieck construction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∫
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int \mathbf{C}
              is locally presentable.
          This follows, as explained in
          = succeed "," do
            %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/102083/381"} MO:a/102083
          %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessibility
          which appears as
          = succeed "." do
            %a{:href => "accessible+category#MakkaiParé1989"} Makkai &amp; Paré (1989), Prop. 5.3.1. (4)
          %h3#combinatorial_model_categories Combinatorial model categories
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            that is in particular a locally presentable category.
          %h3#orthogonal_subcategory_problem Orthogonal subcategory problem
          %p
            Given a class of morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            in a locally presentable category, the answer to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+subcategory+problem"} orthogonal subcategory problem
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\perp
            is affirmative if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is small, and is affirmative for any class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            assuming the large cardinal axiom known as
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vopenka%27s+principle"} Vopenka's principle
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
